DESCRIPTION >
    Banner events deduplicated by (day, banner_id, user_id), keeping the row with
    the latest updated_at. Partitioned by month; because the partition key is a
    function of `day` (the first sorting-key column), duplicate keys can never span
    partitions. That invariant is the prerequisite for
    do_not_merge_across_partitions_select_final, which lets SELECT ... FINAL resolve
    duplicates within each partition independently instead of merging across all of
    them.

    NOTE: that setting is on Tinybird's restricted list and is rejected in both
    ENGINE_SETTINGS and query-level SETTINGS by default. It must be allowlisted at
    the cluster/infra level before it can be applied — the table below is designed
    so it is safe to enable once that's done.

SCHEMA >
    `day` Date `json:$.day`,
    `banner_id` String `json:$.banner_id`,
    `user_id` String `json:$.user_id`,
    `clicked` UInt8 `json:$.clicked`,
    `updated_at` DateTime `json:$.updated_at`

ENGINE "ReplacingMergeTree"
ENGINE_VER "updated_at"
ENGINE_PARTITION_KEY "toYYYYMM(day)"
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY "day, banner_id, user_id"
